                <pb facs="0862" n="726" sameAs="frus:frus1929v01/pg726"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">723.2515/3257a: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Ambassador in Peru</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Moore</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1929-02-11T18:00:00-05:00">February 11, 1929—6
                        p.m.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p>10. The engineers have doubtless returned to Lima now and have presented their
                    report on the situation at Arica to President Leguia. I sincerely hope that he
                    will be able to make a generous and practicable proposal without delay.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Kellogg</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
